      "text": "Rate Limiter",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Rate Limiter",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "cQh0DKVUkxqK--5A1xyG9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 347.7890625,
      "y": -115.3671875,
      "width": 1429.468017578125,
      "height": 387.7159090909089,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1131274027,
      "version": 185,
      "versionNonce": 1695431307,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781903383653,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-- A rate limiter controls how many requests a client can make within a specific timeframe. \nIt acts like a traffic controller for your API -\nallowing, for example, 100 requests per minute from a user, \nthen rejecting excess requests with an HTTP 429 \"Too Many Requests\" response. \nRate limiters prevent abuse, protect your servers from being overwhelmed by bursts of traffic, \nand ensure fair usage across all users.\nExample: \n-- Per-user limits: \"Alice can make 1000 requests/hour\"\n-- Per-IP limits: \"This IP can make 100 requests/minute\"\n-- Global limits: \"Our API can handle 50,000 requests/second total\"\n-- Endpoint-specific limits: \"The search API is limited to 10 requests/minute, but profile updates are 100/minute\"\n",
      "fontSize": 25.84772727272726,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-- A rate limiter controls how many requests a client can make within a specific timeframe. \nIt acts like a traffic controller for your API -\nallowing, for example, 100 requests per minute from a user, \nthen rejecting excess requests with an HTTP 429 \"Too Many Requests\" response. \nRate limiters prevent abuse, protect your servers from being overwhelmed by bursts of traffic, \nand ensure fair usage across all users.\nExample: \n-- Per-user limits: \"Alice can make 1000 requests/hour\"\n-- Per-IP limits: \"This IP can make 100 requests/minute\"\n-- Global limits: \"Our API can handle 50,000 requests/second total\"\n-- Endpoint-specific limits: \"The search API is limited to 10 requests/minute, but profile updates are 100/minute\"\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
