    {
      "id": "musy-6E7TJcwMXTaK7eX_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1996.3397367531106,
      "y": 52.370790370102526,
      "width": 203.119873046875,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 645969893,
      "version": 67,
      "versionNonce": 449583781,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781904940204,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "feed@v21/en.json\nmanifet/en.json\nlocal_graph@v12.yaml",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "feed@v21/en.json\nmanifet/en.json\nlocal_graph@v12.yaml",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5quhOts-4Y0IN6ITjJpZA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 90.81451475149484,
      "y": 1093.7120958188316,
      "width": 1189.8389892578125,
      "height": 1025,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7m",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1546361355,
      "version": 173,
      "versionNonce": 856787205,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781906423713,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** Update/publish path\n\n* PMs/editors change JSON files in GitHub (folders per locale, files per namespace). A push triggers workers.\n* Workers load the root locale (en) and the locale graph, validate ICU syntax, \nand fill missing keys via fallback (hi_IN → hi → en). They compile messages to fast runtime functions.\n* For any namespace/locale that changed, \nworkers bump a version and write immutable, versioned packs to S3: \n/packs/{namespace}/{locale}/{version}.json. Cache-Control is long (immutable, 1y).\n* After all packs are uploaded, workers atomically update a tiny manifest index \n(namespace → locale → version, plus lastUpdated). That’s the only frequently changing file.\n* S3 replicates (CRR/MRAP). CDN fronts S3: packs get long TTL; \nthe index gets a short TTL with ETag/stale‑while‑revalidate.\n If a worker fails mid‑run, the index isn’t updated, so clients keep the old set. Retries/DLQ finish the job later.\n\n\n*** Runtime read path (clients)\n\n* On app start and then every ~20–60s with jitter, clients poll the small manifest index via CDN using If‑None‑Match. \nMost polls return 304.\n* If a needed namespace/locale version changed, the client fetches the new versioned pack URL. \nPacks are cached at the CDN and on device (memory + IndexedDB/SQLite), so fetches are rare and fast.\n* Rendering uses the precompiled message functions. \nPluralization/gender are resolved at render time with parameters. No network on the hot path.\n* Localized assets use the same pattern: versioned, per‑locale URLs in the index (or a parallel assets index). \nRTL locales point to their own assets.\n\n***Server/backends (SSR, emails, jobs)\n\n* Servers call the i18n service with namespace/locale/version. \nThe service does read‑through caching on Redis keyed by the versioned URL. \nOn miss it pulls from S3/CDN, stores in Redis, and returns the pack.\n* Because packs are immutable and versioned, caches use long TTLs without explicit invalidation. \nRolling back is just flipping the version in the index.\n\n\n***Why this works\n\n* Atomicity: packs first, index last, so clients never see partial updates.\n* Performance: tiny index with short TTL, large packs with long TTL. CDN + client caches keep p95 latency low.\n* Consistency: clients switch only when they see the new index; replication lag can’t create mixed states.\n* Scalability: namespaces isolate ownership and allow incremental fetches; versioned URLs keep caches hot across regions.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** Update/publish path\n\n* PMs/editors change JSON files in GitHub (folders per locale, files per namespace). A push triggers workers.\n* Workers load the root locale (en) and the locale graph, validate ICU syntax, \nand fill missing keys via fallback (hi_IN → hi → en). They compile messages to fast runtime functions.\n* For any namespace/locale that changed, \nworkers bump a version and write immutable, versioned packs to S3: \n/packs/{namespace}/{locale}/{version}.json. Cache-Control is long (immutable, 1y).\n* After all packs are uploaded, workers atomically update a tiny manifest index \n(namespace → locale → version, plus lastUpdated). That’s the only frequently changing file.\n* S3 replicates (CRR/MRAP). CDN fronts S3: packs get long TTL; \nthe index gets a short TTL with ETag/stale‑while‑revalidate.\n If a worker fails mid‑run, the index isn’t updated, so clients keep the old set. Retries/DLQ finish the job later.\n\n\n*** Runtime read path (clients)\n\n* On app start and then every ~20–60s with jitter, clients poll the small manifest index via CDN using If‑None‑Match. \nMost polls return 304.\n* If a needed namespace/locale version changed, the client fetches the new versioned pack URL. \nPacks are cached at the CDN and on device (memory + IndexedDB/SQLite), so fetches are rare and fast.\n* Rendering uses the precompiled message functions. \nPluralization/gender are resolved at render time with parameters. No network on the hot path.\n* Localized assets use the same pattern: versioned, per‑locale URLs in the index (or a parallel assets index). \nRTL locales point to their own assets.\n\n***Server/backends (SSR, emails, jobs)\n\n* Servers call the i18n service with namespace/locale/version. \nThe service does read‑through caching on Redis keyed by the versioned URL. \nOn miss it pulls from S3/CDN, stores in Redis, and returns the pack.\n* Because packs are immutable and versioned, caches use long TTLs without explicit invalidation. \nRolling back is just flipping the version in the index.\n\n\n***Why this works\n\n* Atomicity: packs first, index last, so clients never see partial updates.\n* Performance: tiny index with short TTL, large packs with long TTL. CDN + client caches keep p95 latency low.\n* Consistency: clients switch only when they see the new index; replication lag can’t create mixed states.\n* Scalability: namespaces isolate ownership and allow incremental fetches; versioned URLs keep caches hot across regions.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
